(4) BEATER-OBSTRUCTION in cloud terms: to beat, a covering set's phase cloud must clear <n from 0 at EVERY t
    (max clearance < n/Phi6). But covering (multiple of every q<=n) forces the small speeds {1..n-2}, whose
    phases at t* are the AP(step n) -> gap exactly n at 0. So the observer's gap can't shrink below n at t*;
    the killer only SYMMETRIZES it (antipode). This is the S79 Phi6-metric-irreducibility as a CLOUD fact:
    the AP-step is n because the DEEP witness is Phi6 (=n^2-n+1), and the AP of the small speeds tiles Z/Phi6
    with step n, leaving the size-n gap at 0. Covering => AP-step n => clearance n => M >= n/Phi6.

INTEGRATION: covering-min extremizer = an ARITHMETIC-PROGRESSION phase cloud (step n) + an ANTIPODAL KILLER,
observer in the size-n gap, flanked by the 2-point Chebyshev alternation {1, killer}={+n,-n}. Unifies
